{{> page-header}}
<div class="container">
    <div id="purpose" class="mission-statement scrollspy">
        <p class="grey-text text-darken-1"><strong>Regulatory reference:</strong> CYFSA, 2017; O. Reg. 156/18, s. 6 (policies and procedures); MCCSS foster care licence.</p>
        <h2>Purpose</h2>
        <p>This document describes the foster care program operated by Annie&rsquo;s Havens Ltd., including the agency&rsquo;s mission, the children and young persons it serves, the care programs it offers, its service area, and the way services are organized and delivered. It provides a common reference for foster parents, staff, placing agencies, and the Ministry of Children, Community and Social Services.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-links">
        <div class="collection with-header">
            <p class="collection-header"><strong>On this page</strong></p>
            <a href="#mission" class="collection-item">Mission</a>
            <a href="#about" class="collection-item">About Us</a>
            <a href="#population" class="collection-item">Population Served</a>
            <a href="#programs" class="collection-item">Programs</a>
            <a href="#service-area" class="collection-item">Service Area</a>
            <a href="#referrals" class="collection-item">Referrals</a>
            <a href="#supports" class="collection-item">Supports</a>
            <a href="#foster-parents" class="collection-item">Foster Parents</a>
            <a href="#organization" class="collection-item">Organization</a>
            <a href="#philosophy" class="collection-item">Philosophy</a>
            <a href="#compliance" class="collection-item">Compliance</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="mission" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">flag</i>
                <span class="card-title">Mission Statement</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens has a total commitment to quality and excellence in everything it does. The agency will provide a positive growth environment for every child and young person placed in its care. To accomplish this, Annie&rsquo;s Havens gives careful attention to the matching and placement of each child, and provides exceptional support and specialized training to its foster parents and staff.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="about" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">history_edu</i>
                <span class="card-title">About Annie&rsquo;s Havens</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens Ltd. is a licensed private foster care agency that has provided foster care in Ontario since 1996. The agency was founded by William and Hilda Wilson, who had been foster parents since the early 1990s, and is named in memory of their daughter, Annie. The family&rsquo;s experience caring for Annie, who lived with significant physical and medical needs, gave Annie&rsquo;s Havens its founding expertise in caring for children with special needs, and that focus remains at the heart of the agency today.</p>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens is licensed by the Ministry of Children, Community and Social Services (MCCSS) and operates as a foster care licensee under the Child, Youth and Family Services Act, 2017 (CYFSA) and its regulations. The agency receives referrals from Children&rsquo;s Aid Societies and other placing agencies across its service area.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="population" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">diversity_3</i>
                <span class="card-title">Population Served</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens provides foster care to children and young persons who are in the care of, or are being placed by, Children&rsquo;s Aid Societies and other authorized placing agencies. Children come into care for many reasons and arrive with a range of needs, from comparatively low-needs placements to children with complex developmental, physical, and medical requirements. Annie&rsquo;s Havens is particularly recognized for its work with children who have special needs.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="programs" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">list_alt</i>
                <span class="card-title">Foster Care Programs</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens offers a range of foster care programs so that placements can be matched to the needs of each child or young person.</p>
            <ul class="collapsible">
                <li class="active">
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="pd-prog-header-1" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="pd-prog-body-1">Mainstream<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="pd-prog-body-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="pd-prog-header-1">
                        <p>The mainstream program serves children and young persons who present with comparatively lower needs and a low degree of trauma-related behaviours. All children in care arrive with some degree of trauma and unique considerations, and the agency&rsquo;s training prepares foster parents to understand and respond to expected behaviours through a supportive lens. Mainstream foster parents are encouraged to build their skills over time so that they can care for children with more complex needs.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="pd-prog-header-2" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pd-prog-body-2">Special Needs<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="pd-prog-body-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="pd-prog-header-2">
                        <p>The special needs program is the core of Annie&rsquo;s Havens and the reason the agency was created. It serves children and young persons with developmental, physical, and medical needs. Foster parents in this program are committed, experienced caregivers, and Annie&rsquo;s Havens provides specialized training and, where required, Personal Support Worker (PSW) hours to support higher care needs in the home. Backgrounds such as nursing, personal support work, or caring for a family member are valuable in this program.</p>
                        <p>The spectrum of special needs served includes, but is not limited to:</p>
                        <ul class="browser-default">
                            <li>mobility needs (for example, wheelchair or walker use);</li>
                            <li>Autism Spectrum Disorder;</li>
                            <li>global developmental delays;</li>
                            <li>tube or intravenous feeding (for example, G-tube or TPN);</li>
                            <li>medically fragile children; and</li>
                            <li>palliative care.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Because adoption and permanency planning can take considerably longer for children with special needs, foster parents in this program are prepared to provide care over an extended period.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="collapsible-header" id="pd-prog-header-3" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pd-prog-body-3">Trauma-Focused Care<i class="collapsible-secondary material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">arrow_drop_down</i></div>
                    <div class="collapsible-body" id="pd-prog-body-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="pd-prog-header-3">
                        <p>Trauma-focused care for children and young persons with significant trauma-related needs is provided through Annie&rsquo;s Havens&rsquo; sister agency, Safe Harbours Family Treatment Homes. Trauma-focused foster parents have a background in child psychology, behavioural therapy, or a Child and Youth Worker credential, and complete a specialized trauma-focused curriculum before a home is licensed, with ongoing in-service training. Where a referral calls for trauma-focused treatment care, Annie&rsquo;s Havens coordinates with Safe Harbours. Further information about the Safe Harbours program is available at <a href="https://safeharbours.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">safeharbours.ca</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>Learn more about each program on our <a href="/care-programs">Care Programs</a> page.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="service-area" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">map</i>
                <span class="card-title">Service Area</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens maintains a defined service area of more than 30,000 square kilometres across southern and central Ontario, extending from Woodstock in the southwest to Peterborough in the east and north to Gravenhurst. A defined service area allows the agency to concentrate its resources, including in-home staff support and responsive travel time in the event of an emergency. Homes outside the service area may be considered on a case-by-case basis depending on the circumstances.</p>
            <p>See our <a href="/service-area">Service Area</a> page for more detail.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="referrals" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">how_to_reg</i>
                <span class="card-title">Referrals and Admission</span>
            </div>
            <p>Referrals are received from Children&rsquo;s Aid Societies and other placing agencies. Before any child or young person is placed, Annie&rsquo;s Havens completes a pre-placement assessment to determine whether the child&rsquo;s immediate needs can be met in the proposed foster home, in accordance with the agency&rsquo;s Placement of Children and Youth policy and the requirements of O. Reg. 156/18. Placement decisions consider the needs and identity of the child, the suitability and training of the foster home, and the needs of any children already residing in the home.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="supports" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">volunteer_activism</i>
                <span class="card-title">Supports and Services</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens wraps services around each placement based on the assessed needs of the child or young person. Depending on those needs, supports may include:</p>
            <ul class="browser-default">
                <li>Personal Support Workers for children with higher daily care needs;</li>
                <li>Child and Youth Workers;</li>
                <li>access to community mental health services and, where needed, funding for psychological services;</li>
                <li>educational supports, including liaison with the school board and tutoring; and</li>
                <li>access to community support programs.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>A preliminary assessment of a child&rsquo;s support needs is completed early in the placement so that any additional in-home support can be arranged.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="foster-parents" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">school</i>
                <span class="card-title">Foster Parent Recruitment, Training, and Support</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens recruits, assesses, approves, and supports foster parents in accordance with its assessment, screening, and approval policies and the requirements of the CYFSA and O. Reg. 156/18. Foster parents complete pre-service qualifications and a learning plan, receive program-specific and in-service training, and are supported by agency staff through regular contact, in-home support, and ongoing professional development.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="organization" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">account_tree</i>
                <span class="card-title">Organizational Structure and Staffing</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens is led by an Executive Director and a Director of Children&rsquo;s Services, supported by a Compliance Manager, Case Managers, a Placement Coordinator, a Director of Service Development, and Area Managers. Resource Workers and Case Managers maintain regular contact with foster homes, monitor the well-being of children in care, and ensure compliance with agency policy and legislation. Staffing levels and roles are maintained to support the safe operation of the program across the service area.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="philosophy" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">psychology</i>
                <span class="card-title">Service Philosophy and Approach</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens is committed to child-centred, trauma-informed, and culturally responsive care that protects the dignity, safety, and rights of every child and young person. The agency emphasizes prevention, relationship-based care, and de-escalation. Annie&rsquo;s Havens is a hands-off provider: physical restraint is prohibited in all Annie&rsquo;s Havens foster homes, as set out in the Physical Restraints policy, and behaviour is supported through the strategies described in the agency&rsquo;s behaviour support and safety planning policies.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="compliance" class="card scrollspy">
        <div class="card-content">
            <div class="row valign-wrapper">
                <i class="medium material-symbols-outlined circle blue-grey white-text" aria-hidden="true">gavel</i>
                <span class="card-title">Legislative Compliance</span>
            </div>
            <p>Annie&rsquo;s Havens operates in compliance with the Child, Youth and Family Services Act, 2017 and its regulations, the Personal Health Information Protection Act, 2004 (PHIPA), and the requirements of its MCCSS foster care licence. All services are delivered in keeping with the rights of children and young persons in care and the agency&rsquo;s policies and procedures.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

